{"event_type":"finding-event","id":"b28a17d14b86b13bb7d6208f1e192d064ff883952935d6fbd40945e3656b39df","occurred_at":"2026-11-09T02:08:56Z","payload":{"action":"confirmed","actor":"crq-triage/opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash","evidence":{"anchor_recovered_from":"e9f7ea515e882ae1017075956295b922d8b3b709da95abfdd5a75272c23eb32f","anchor_verified":true,"mapped_intervals":[[130,131]],"mapped_path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts","quoted_text":"        input: structuredClone(job.input),\n        inputsHash: hashInputs(job.op, job.input),","reason":"At the pinned tip, makeManifest validates and hashes `job.input` directly but stores a separate `structuredClone(job.input)`. A plain object with accessor properties can return different values across those reads, so the stored `input` can differ from the input hashed in `inputsHash`. This violates the function's stated invariant that the committed hash is the hash of the dispatched input snapshot. The code has no guard rejecting accessors before hashing.","recovered_anchor":{"anchor_recovered_from":"e9f7ea515e882ae1017075956295b922d8b3b709da95abfdd5a75272c23eb32f","blob":"52ba9c56f4799da5ef9bd98206229ca41f2b0821","intervals":[[131,131]],"path":"src/kernel/manifest.ts"},"target":"641bc7a7419955d4b77a5a87bcdb79b4dfda5af2"},"finding_id":"ec188a7705e86962d871ae991258b8277cd3e3a1654b574231ba58f4c57b2ad0","previous_event_id":null,"review_id":"899cff93c770e74d3d7ec07e8dd0fc65eda21bc441bca6e88c363c64b29ea4d9"},"schema":"cq.review-ledger/v1","source_key":"finding:ec188a7705e86962d871ae991258b8277cd3e3a1654b574231ba58f4c57b2ad0:eaa1cf24be6725a93f8b935edecd92e5248cb97774e94c8a4844b29e996010cc"}